WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.640 line:80%
Reading about SQL injection is not
the same as seeing the check that fails.

00:00:08.585 --> 00:00:12.745 line:80%
These exercises put application behavior
in front of students,

00:00:12.755 --> 00:00:17.975 line:80%
with separate directories
for SQL injection, loose PHP comparisons,

00:00:18.135 --> 00:00:21.735 line:80%
regular expressions
and token authentication.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.450 line:80%
Students can inspect the PHP
and JavaScript

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.570 line:80%
beside the page assets and the SQL files,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.930 line:80%
and a small form makes its input explicit.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.810 line:80%
What matters is the comparison:
the code takes the input as trusted,

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.820 line:80%
then checks it with a loose match.

00:00:42.315 --> 00:00:43.925 line:80%
The published implementation

00:00:44.145 --> 00:00:47.895 line:80%
gives a classroom lab concrete
source material to examine.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:54.300 line:80%
The exercises appear here
as source and page material;

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:57.910 line:80%
no live attack is performed
against a running target.

00:00:58.565 --> 00:01:00.535 line:80%
The source stays visible:

00:01:00.545 --> 00:01:03.935 line:80%
that is what gives the classroom
something concrete to discuss.
